<p>When upgrading the printer driver, uninstall the old version before 
 installing the new one.</p>
<h2>Uninstalling the Printer Driver</h2>
<p>This describes how to uninstall the printer driver and delete any custom 
 settings registered. If you want to use any existing custom settings after 
 the upgrade, save them as a printer properties settings file before you 
 start.</p>
<p>For details about saving and registering One Click Preset, see <a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_ONECLICK_EXPORT">Saving 
 a Registered One Click Preset as a File</a> and <a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_ONECLICK_IMPORT">Loading 
 a Printing Preferences Settings File as a One Click Preset</a>.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, select the icon of the printer you want to delete.</p></li>
<li><p>Right click the selected printer icon, and then 
 click <span class="Term-OS">Remove device</span>. </p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If multiple 
 drivers are registered on one printer icon, click <span class="Term-OS">Delete 
 print queue</span> and select the driver to delete.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="3">
<li><p>When a confirmation message appears, click <span class="Term-OS">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>The printer icon is deleted.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a printer icon, and then click <span class="Term-OS">Print 
 server properties</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>On the <span class="Term-OS">Drivers</span> tab 
 in the <span class="Term-OS">Print Server Properties</span> dialog box, 
 select the printer you want to delete, and then click <span class="Term-OS">Remove...</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Restart Windows.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Installing the New Printer Driver</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, click <span class="Term-OS">Add a printer</span>.<br/>
 Follow the instructions given by the printer wizard.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">When the dialog 
 box asking for the machine manufacturer and model appears, click <span class="Term-OS">Have Disk...</span> and specify the directory containing 
 the new printer driver files.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">When you are 
 asked to keep the existing driver or to replace the existing driver with 
 the new driver, click <span class="Term-OS">Replace existing driver</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>When installation is completed, restart Windows.</p></li>
<li><p>Configure installed options and paper trays.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">This is only 
 necessary if bidirectional communication is not operating.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
